<h2>Where should the activity filters go?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Same controls in each: two presets (Failed sign-ins, Security changes), nine event-type checkboxes, a start and end date, and a live result count. Only placement differs.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 6px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:8px">
            <div style="display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px">
              <button class="mock-button">Failed sign-ins</button>
              <button class="mock-button">Security changes</button>
            </div>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end">
              <div class="placeholder" style="flex:2;min-width:120px">Event type: 9 checkboxes in 3 columns</div>
              <input class="mock-input" placeholder="From" style="width:70px">
              <input class="mock-input" placeholder="To" style="width:70px">
            </div>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 4px;font-size:0.8em">Showing 6 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table (full width)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>A. Filter panel above the table</h3>
      <p>Everything visible at once. Full-width table. Stacks naturally at 320px. Pushes the table down by roughly the panel's height.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 6px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin-bottom:6px">
            <button class="mock-button">Failed sign-ins</button>
            <button class="mock-button">Security changes</button>
            <input class="mock-input" placeholder="From" style="width:70px">
            <input class="mock-input" placeholder="To" style="width:70px">
            <button class="mock-button">Event types (9) &#9662;</button>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:4px;margin-bottom:6px"><span class="label">Sign-in failed &times;</span></div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 4px;font-size:0.8em">Showing 6 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table (full width)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>B. Compact toolbar, types in a popover</h3>
      <p>One row; checkboxes open in a popover; active types show as removable tags. Table stays high on the page. More JS (popover open/close, focus return, Escape) and a bigger diff.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
